.TH ALFE 1 "May 2026" "alfe 1.0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
alfe \- AutoLISP front-end driving clautolisp, BricsCAD or AutoCAD.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B alfe
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ FILE.lsp ]
.br
.B alfe
.B \-\-clautolisp
.RI [ options ]
.B \-l
.I FILE
.br
.B alfe
.B \-\-bricscad
.RI [ options ]
.B \-x
.I EXPR
.br
.B alfe
.B \-\-autocad
.RI [ options ]
.B \-\-dwg
.I DRAWING.dwg
.B \-l
.I script.lsp
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B alfe
is a single CLI front-end that drives an AutoLISP runtime against
one of three backends: the in-process or subprocess clautolisp
evaluator, or a CAD-resident engine (BricsCAD / AutoCAD) over a
file-IPC protocol. It accepts the standard option vocabulary
.RB ( \-l ", " \-x ", " \-i ", " \-\-dialect ", " \-\-host ", "
.BR \-e ", " \-E ", " \-\-no-init ", " \-\-no-color "), "
plus a handful of CAD-specific knobs
.RB ( \-\-mode ", " \-\-backend ", " \-\-dwg ", "
.BR \-\-workdir ", " \-\-keep-workdir ", " \-\-timeout ", "
.BR \-\-bootstrap-phase ", " \-\-main ", " \-\-quit ", " \-\-dry-run ).
Behaviour that belongs to one site, one CAD product or one user is added by
plug-ins, which define options of their own (see
.BR PLUG-INS ).
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Backend selection (mutually exclusive)
.TP
.B \-\-clautolisp
Default. Drive
.BR clautolisp (1)
in-process or as a subprocess.
.TP
.B \-\-bricscad
Drive BricsCAD via the file-IPC protocol.
.TP
.B \-\-autocad
Drive AutoCAD via the file-IPC protocol.
.SS Mode and variant
.TP
.BR \-\-mode " " \fI{auto,automation,batch}\fR
How to launch the engine (default: auto).
.TP
.BR \-\-backend " " \fI{attach,launch,direct,subprocess}\fR
CAD backends: attach to a running CAD or launch a fresh one.
Under
.BR \-\-clautolisp :
.B direct
(the default) runs the clautolisp engine inside alfe,
.B subprocess
runs the clautolisp executable as a child. The two are transports for one
engine: every option accepted with
.B \-\-clautolisp
has the same meaning, output, diagnostics and exit status under both
(the subprocess engine receives alfe's resolved
.B *AUTOLISP\-...*
values). A run that needs the clautolisp program itself \(em a REPL
.RB ( \-i ,
or no action), a recording
.RB ( \-\-dribble ),
.B \-\-dcl ncurses
or
.BR gui ,
.B \-\-host cadtui
\(em runs the clautolisp executable as a child even without
.BR "\-\-backend subprocess" ,
so both spellings behave identically; with
.B \-\-backend direct
it is a usage error.
.SS Actions (processed in order)
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-load " " \fIFILE\fR
Load and evaluate FILE.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-eval " " \fIEXPR\fR
Evaluate EXPR.
.TP
.BR \-\-main " " \fIFN\fR
Call FN as the script entry point after loading.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interactive
Drop into a REPL after the action queue. Under
.B \-\-clautolisp
it is the clautolisp REPL (interactors, comma commands, the aldo debugger),
run in the clautolisp executable.
.TP
.B \-\-quit
Force the engine to shut down after the queue.
.SS Dialect, host, encoding
.TP
.BR \-\-dialect " " \fINAME\fR
.BR strict " (default), " autocad-2026 ", " bricscad-v26 ", " clautolisp .
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " \fINAME\fR
Host backend of the clautolisp backend (the CAD backends are their own host):
.B cador
(default), the headless in-memory CAD core;
.BR cadtui ,
the textual UI-tree host; or
.BR nihil ,
no host at all. alfe passes the choice on to clautolisp. Because cadtui is
provided by the clautolisp executable rather than by alfe's embedded engine,
.B \-\-host cadtui
runs the engine as a child process, as
.BR "\-\-backend subprocess" ;
with
.B \-\-backend direct
it is a usage error.
.TP
.BR \-e " " \fIENC\fR
Source-file encoding (case-insensitive). Accepts
.BR \-mac " / " \-dos " / " \-unix " / " \-lf " / " \-cr " / " \-crlf
line-terminator suffixes. Run
.B alfe \-\-list-encodings
for the catalogue.
.TP
.BR \-E " " \fIENC\fR
Declared terminal-IO encoding. Accepted-and-ignored on the
terminal side (line-buffered by default).
.SS CAD-specific options
.TP
.BR \-\-dwg " " \fIFILE\fR
Drawing to open before running the script.
.TP
.BR \-\-cad " " \fIDENOTATION\fR
Pick a specific installed CAD by its canonical denotation
.RI ( acad-2026 ", " bricscad-v25-fr_FR ", " autocad-2022 ", ...).
.TP
.B \-\-list-cad-programs
Scan the host for installed CADs, print each with its canonical
denotation, and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-print-command
Stage the workdir for real, print the CAD command line that would be
launched, and launch nothing. CAD backends only.
.TP
.BR \-\-cad-log " " \fIFILE\fR
.BR \-\-autocad " / " \-\-bricscad :
after the run, copy the CAD's own command-history log
.RB ( LOGFILEMODE ,
which alfe directs into its workdir) to FILE in UTF-8, decoded per
.BR \-Elog ,
else as measured: a byte-order mark's encoding, windows-1252 on
MS-Windows, auto-detected elsewhere. No log (BricsCAD on macOS in batch
mode), or the clautolisp backend: a warning, and no file.
.TP
.BR \-\-write-workdir-path " " \fIFILE\fR
After the workdir is prepared, write its absolute path to FILE, one
line. Lets a caller locate a
.B \-\-keep-workdir
workdir without scraping stdout. Honoured equivalently via
.BR $AUTOLISP_WRITE_WORKDIR_PATH .
.TP
.BR \-\-dcl " " \fIMODE\fR
.BR \-\-clautolisp :
the DCL renderer, as clautolisp's
.BR \-\-dcl :
.BR tui " (the line form), " ncurses ", " gui " (the " $CLAUTOLISP_GUI " driver) or " auto
(the default).
.B ncurses
and
.B gui
run the clautolisp executable on alfe's terminal.
.SS Recording a session
.TP
.BR \-\-dribble " [=" \fIFILE\fR ]
Record the session's interactions into a log file: the forms alfe sends, the
engine's output
.RB ( ";; O: " ),
its error output
.RB ( ";; E: " ),
and condition reports
.RB ( ";; C: " ).
Bare, the file is
.IR $XDG_STATE_HOME/alfe/dribbles/<backend>/<timestamp>.log ;
with
.IR =FILE ,
that file, appended to when it exists. The header names both versions:
.RB ` ";; H: alfe " \fIVERSION\fR " " \fIBACKEND\fR " " \fICAD-VERSION\fR '.
.IP
Under
.B \-\-clautolisp
the request is FORWARDED to the clautolisp executable, which records its own
REPL \(em a richer transcript than alfe could reconstruct, and only one file
per session; a batch run, having no REPL, records nothing, as with
.BR clautolisp .
Under
.BR \-\-autocad / \-\-bricscad
alfe records what it sees, because those engines have no dribble of their own.
.TP
.BR \-\-dribble-interactors " " \fIIS\fR
Which interactors are recorded:
.B t
for all, or a comma-separated list of names. Meaningful for
.B \-\-clautolisp
only, where interactors exist, and forwarded there; the CAD backends have no
interactor stack and record the whole session.
.SS Bootstrap and runtime
.TP
.BR \-\-bootstrap-phase " " \fI{marker,core,log,full}\fR
Truncate the bootstrap.
.TP
.BR \-\-workdir " " \fIDIR\fR
Override
.BR $AUTOLISP_WORKDIR .
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECS\fR
Per-action timeout.
.TP
.BR \-\-no-init ", " \-norc
Skip user init files. Honoured equivalently via
.BR $AUTOLISP_NO_INIT " / " $ALFE_NO_INIT .
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI colour. Honoured equivalently via
.BR $NO_COLOR .
.TP
.B \-\-keep-workdir
Keep the engine workdir at end of run (do not delete). Honoured
equivalently via
.BR $AUTOLISP_KEEP_WORKDIR .
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print the resolved action plan and exit 0.
.SS Plug-ins
.TP
.BR \-\-plugin " " \fINAME\fR
Activate the installed plug-in NAME (repeatable). Mirrors
.BR $ALFE_PLUGINS .
.TP
.BR \-\-plugin-path " " \fIDIR\fR
Add DIR to the plug-in search path (repeatable). Mirrors
.BR $ALFE_PLUGIN_PATH .
.TP
.B \-\-no-plugins
Load no plug-in. Mirrors
.BR $ALFE_NO_PLUGINS .
.TP
.B \-\-list-plugins
Print the installed plug-ins and the search path, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-\-compile-plugin " " \fIFILE\fR
Compile the plug-in source FILE for this alfe, then exit. The result is
written next to FILE; the exit status is 0, or 1 on a compile error.
.PP
.B \-\-help
ends with a generated
.RB \(lq "Plug-in options" \(rq
section listing every option of every installed plug-in. The options below
are defined by the plug-ins that ship with alfe. Apart from the one that
activates its plug-in, each is a usage error while that plug-in is not
active.
.SS "EPURE plug-in options"
.TP
.B \-\-epure
Activate the
.B epure
plug-in: launch BricsCAD or AutoCAD under the EPURE profile, from the CAD's
.B UserDataCache
directory, and run EPURE's control script before alfe's own runtime is
loaded. MS-Windows only, with
.B \-\-bricscad
or
.BR \-\-autocad ;
silently ignored on other systems and under
.BR \-\-clautolisp .
With
.B \-\-autocad
it refuses
.BR "\-\-mode batch" .
Mirrors
.BR $AUTOLISP_EPURE .
.TP
.BR \-\-epure-profile " " \fINAME\fR
CAD user profile to run under (default:
.BR Epure ).
Mirrors
.BR $AUTOLISP_EPURE_PROFILE .
.TP
.BR \-\-epure-script " " \fIFILE\fR
EPURE control script. Default, for BricsCAD:
.br
.B %APPDATA%\esncf\eepure\eepure\ 2022_b\econtrol_path_epure_2022.scr
.br
and for AutoCAD:
.br
.B %APPDATA%\esncf\eepure\eepure\ 2022\econtrol_path_epure_2022.scr
.br
Mirrors
.BR $AUTOLISP_EPURE_SCRIPT .
.SS "EPUREE plug-in options"
.TP
.B \-\-epuree
Activate the
.B epuree
plug-in: load the EPUREE emulation of the EPURE API, through ALPM, before
anything else the action plan does (it shows in
.BR \-\-dry-run ).
Every backend, every system. Mirrors
.BR $AUTOLISP_EPUREE .
.TP
.BR \-\-epuree-path " " \fIDIR\fR
Register DIR, searched recursively, with ALPM as holding
.BR epuree.alpm
(repeatable). Mirrors
.BR $EPUREE_PATH ,
a PATH-style list.
.TP
.BR \-\-epuree-alpm " " \fIFILE\fR
The
.B alpm.lsp
to load. By default it is looked for in
.BR $ALPM_LSP ,
.BR PREFIX/share/autolisp/ ,
.BR /opt/local/share/autolisp/ ,
.B /usr/local/share/autolisp/
and
.BR ~/.local/share/autolisp/ ;
when it is nowhere, alfe exits 69 (EX_UNAVAILABLE) listing the places
tried (66, EX_NOINPUT, when the file named is not there). Mirrors
.BR $ALPM_LSP .
.SS Diagnostics
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose progress.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress non-error output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Debug traces (implies
.BR \-\-verbose ).
.TP
.SS Debugger (aldo)
The debugger options of
.BR clautolisp (1),
with the same spelling, values and meaning. Under
.B \-\-clautolisp
both engine variants apply them: the in-process engine
.RB ( "\-\-backend direct" )
starts the aldo session exactly as the clautolisp program does, and the
subprocess variant forwards them to the clautolisp child, which then runs on
alfe's terminal when they start a debugger. The CAD backends have no aldo:
.B \-\-autocad
and
.B \-\-bricscad
refuse all of them but
.B \-\-on-error
with a usage error (EX_USAGE, 64).
.TP
.BI \-\-on-error " POLICY"
An uncaught AutoLISP error under
.BR \-\-clautolisp :
.B quit
reports it and exits 1 (the default of a batch run),
.B debug
stops in the aldo debugger at the error (the default of an interactive REPL),
.B ignore
uses no debugger (the AutoLISP
.B *error*
handler runs). Under every backend,
.B debug
and
.B ignore
also make alfe dump the Common\-Lisp backtrace of an unexpected condition in
alfe itself, captured before the stack unwinds.
.TP
.BI \-\-on-interrupt " POLICY"
Control\-C (SIGINT) under
.BR \-\-clautolisp :
.B debug
(break into aldo at the interrupt point, the default),
.B ignore
(execution resumes) or
.B quit
(exit 130). A second Control\-C while one is being handled exits at once.
In the subprocess variant alfe leaves Control\-C to the child (passing it on
when the terminal did not deliver it).
.TP
.BI \-\-on-quit " POLICY"
.B (quit)
and
.B (exit)
under
.BR \-\-clautolisp :
.B quit
(the default) or
.B debug
(enter aldo before the stack unwinds).
.TP
.BI \-\-debugger-ui " UI"
The aldo front end:
.B dumb
(aliases
.BR terminal ", " tui ),
.BR ncurses ,
or
.B aldb
(alias
.BR emacs ).
Selecting one debugs the run.
.TP
.BI \-\-aldb-listen " [HOST:]PORT"
The address the aldb (Emacs) listener binds; HOST defaults to 127.0.0.1,
PORT 0 picks a free port. Implies
.BR "\-\-debugger-ui aldb" .
.TP
.B \-\-aldb-stdio
aldb over the process's standard input and output. Implies
.BR "\-\-debugger-ui aldb" ;
excludes
.B \-\-interactive
and
.BR \-\-aldb-listen .
.SS Informational
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-encodings
Print every encoding name accepted by
.BR \-e " / " \-E
and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-list-hosts
Print the
.B \-\-host
backends \(em cador, cadtui, nihil \(em with a one-line summary each, and
exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_WORKDIR\fR, \fBAUTOLISP_WAIT_SECS\fR, \fBAUTOLISP_MODE
Defaults for
.BR \-\-workdir ", " \-\-timeout ", " \-\-mode .
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_BACKEND\fR, \fBALFE_BACKEND_OVERRIDE
Backend selector defaults; explicit
.BR \-\-clautolisp " / " \-\-bricscad " / " \-\-autocad
overrides.
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_BOOTSTRAP_PHASE\fR, \fBAUTOLISP_DWG
CAD-side defaults.
.TP
.B ALFE_CLAUTOLISP_BIN
The
.B clautolisp-sbcl
executable run by
.B \-\-backend subprocess
(and
.BR "\-\-host cadtui" ).
Unset or empty,
.B alfe
looks, in order, for
.B clautolisp-sbcl
(\fBclautolisp-sbcl.exe\fR on MS-Windows) in the directory of the running
alfe image, in
.IB PREFIX /libexec/clautolisp/binaries/ OS / CPU /
of the prefix that image is installed in (derived from the image's own
location, so any prefix works, from any current directory), in the
checkout alfe was built from when it still exists, on
.BR $PATH ,
and in
.BR /usr/local/bin ;
the NO-SUBPROCESS-BINARY error lists every place tried.
.TP
.B ALFE_PLUGIN_PATH
Extra plug-in roots, a PATH-style list (separated by colons, or by
semicolons on MS-Windows), searched after the
.B \-\-plugin-path
directories.
.TP
.B ALFE_PLUGINS
Comma-separated names of the plug-ins to activate in every run, like
.B \-\-plugin
once per name.
.TP
.B ALFE_NO_PLUGINS
When set to a true value, load no plug-in, like
.BR \-\-no-plugins .
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_EPURE\fR, \fBAUTOLISP_EPURE_PROFILE\fR, \fBAUTOLISP_EPURE_SCRIPT
Defaults for
.BR \-\-epure ", " \-\-epure-profile ", " \-\-epure-script .
A true value in
.B AUTOLISP_EPURE
activates the
.B epure
plug-in.
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_EPUREE\fR, \fBEPUREE_PATH\fR, \fBALPM_LSP
Defaults for
.BR \-\-epuree ", " \-\-epuree-path ", " \-\-epuree-alpm .
A true value in
.B AUTOLISP_EPUREE
activates the
.B epuree
plug-in.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_DATA_DIRS
Read for the plug-in roots (see
.BR PLUG-INS ).
.TP
.B BRICSCAD_EXE\fR, \fBAUTOCAD_EXE\fR, \fBAUTOCAD_ACCORECONSOLE
Explicit Windows CAD binary overrides. When unset,
.B alfe
searches the standard
.B Program Files
roots for BricsCAD, AutoCAD and
.BR accoreconsole.exe .
.TP
.B AUTOCAD_PROGID
The COM ProgID
.B \-\-mode automation
asks Windows for, used verbatim. Unset,
.B alfe
resolves the selected release's own ProgID
.RB ( AutoCAD.Application.24.1
for AutoCAD 2022) and refuses to fall back to the generic
.B AutoCAD.Application
when a release was named explicitly, since that registration may belong
to a different release.
.TP
.B AUTOLISP_KEEP_WORKDIR
Keep the engine workdir after run.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable ANSI colour output.
.SH PLUG-INS
A plug-in is a Common Lisp file, loaded when alfe starts, that defines
command-line options and may intervene, through named hooks, at every stage
of a run: read and change the parsed options, veto a backend, rewrite the
action plan, add lines to the scripts alfe generates for the CAD, change the
command line and working directory the CAD is launched with, and observe
every action, the shutdown, the exit code and every error.
.PP
Every installed plug-in is loaded, so that its options exist when the command
line is parsed, but only an active plug-in takes part in a run. A plug-in is
active when its own option is given (for instance
.BR \-\-epure ),
or its environment variable holds a true value, or
.B \-\-plugin
names it, or
.B $ALFE_PLUGINS
lists it. With no plug-in active, alfe behaves as if plug-ins did not exist.
An option of a plug-in that is not active is a usage error (exit status 64)
naming the option that activates it.
.B \-\-no-plugins
loads none. A plug-in that fails to load is reported on standard error as
.RB \(lq "alfe: warning: plug-in NAME (PATH): MESSAGE" \(rq
and skipped; an error raised by one of its hooks during a run exits with
status 70 (EX_SOFTWARE). A plug-in runs with alfe's own privileges: there is no sandbox.
.PP
The plug-in
.I NAME
is installed in a plug-in root, a directory with one sub-directory per
plug-in, as
.B NAME/NAME.lisp
(source) or
.B NAME/NAME.VERSION\-IMPL.plugin
(compiled by
.BR \-\-compile-plugin
for alfe version VERSION and the Common Lisp implementation IMPL,
.B sbcl
or
.BR ccl ).
The compiled file is loaded when it is at least as new as the source;
a compiled file for another version or implementation is ignored.
The roots are searched in this order, and the first plug-in of a given name
wins:
.IP 1. 3
each
.B \-\-plugin-path
directory, in command-line order;
.IP 2. 3
each entry of
.BR $ALFE_PLUGIN_PATH ;
.IP 3. 3
.B $XDG_DATA_HOME/clautolisp/plug-in
.RB ( ~/.local/share/clautolisp/plug-in
if unset;
.B %APPDATA%\eclautolisp\eplug\-in
on MS-Windows);
.IP 4. 3
.B clautolisp/plug-in
under each entry of
.B $XDG_DATA_DIRS
.RB ( /usr/local/share:/usr/share
if unset);
.IP 5. 3
.B PREFIX/share/clautolisp/plug-in\fR,
PREFIX being the installation prefix of the running executable.
.B make install
puts the plug-ins that ship with alfe there, and compiles them.
.PP
The plug-ins that ship with alfe are
.B epure
(BricsCAD and AutoCAD under the EPURE profile, MS-Windows only) and
.B epuree
(the EPUREE emulation of the EPURE API, loaded through ALPM). The
.B epure
plug-in has not been validated on real CAD installations.
See the user manual for the complete description, and for how to write a
plug-in.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
Apart from 1,
.I N
and 130, the codes of
.BR sysexits.h ,
with the same values on every system, MS-Windows included. Under
.B \-\-clautolisp
both engine variants give the same status.
.TP
.BR 0 " (EX_OK)"
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The AutoLISP program failed: a runtime error, on any backend.
.TP
.I N
Under
.BR \-\-clautolisp ,
the
.I N
of
.BI "(exit " N )
/
.BI "(quit " N )
or of
.BR autolisp\-set\-status ,
unchanged.
.TP
.BR 64 " (EX_USAGE)"
Usage error: unknown option, missing argument, invalid value,
conflicting options, a plug-in option without its plug-in,
.B \-\-dwg
on a host without drawings.
.TP
.BR 65 " (EX_DATAERR)"
A
.B \-l
file or
.B \-x
expression the reader refuses; a
.B \-\-dwg
file that is not a drawing; a
.B \-\-compile\-plugin
source that does not compile.
.TP
.BR 66 " (EX_NOINPUT)"
An input file does not exist or is not readable: the
.B \-l
file, the
.B \-\-dwg
drawing, the
.B \-\-epuree\-alpm
file, the
.B \-\-compile\-plugin
source.
.TP
.BR 69 " (EX_UNAVAILABLE)"
The backend or something it needs is not there: the CAD program, the
clautolisp executable, accoreconsole, EPURE, alpm.lsp, the DWG native
library; or the CAD could not be brought up.
.TP
.BR 70 " (EX_SOFTWARE)"
Internal error, including an error raised by a plug-in hook.
.TP
.BR 71 " (EX_OSERR)"
The clautolisp child process could not be started.
.TP
.BR 73 " (EX_CANTCREAT)"
The workdir, or the
.B \-\-dribble
transcript, cannot be created.
.TP
.BR 74 " (EX_IOERR)"
Input/output error.
.TP
.BR 75 " (EX_TEMPFAIL)"
The CAD did not answer in time (READY, a request, the shutdown), or a
protocol slot stayed busy; retrying may succeed.
.TP
.BR 76 " (EX_PROTOCOL)"
The CAD runtime answered something the protocol does not allow.
.TP
.B 130
Interrupted (Control-C, 128 + SIGINT).
.PP
Before alfe 2.2.159 the codes were 1, 2 (usage, or a file the engine
could not open), 3 (backend not available) and 4 (bootstrap, protocol
or plug-in error); scripts testing for them must be adapted.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clautolisp (1).
.PP
Full documentation as info pages:
.B info alfe-user-manual
or
.B info alfe-specifications .
.SH AUTHOR
Pascal J. Bourguignon and contributors.
.SH BUGS
Report at https://gitlab.com/informatimago/lisp/-/issues.
